<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merobaudes (general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 383 or 388</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Flavius Merobaudes (consul 377)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merobaudes-poet">Flavius Merobaudes</a> was a Roman general, probably of Frankish origin, who served the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i">Valentinian I</a> and Gratian. In 375 he helped proclaim the child <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-ii">Valentinian II</a> emperor, and he held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">consulship</a> in 377 and 383. He died, probably forced to take his own life, after the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-maximus">Magnus Maximus</a> seized power in the west.</p></div>
